ds.vibe_query:
I'm having an issue with adding comments to Jira issues through our Go client. When serializing the comment data to JSON, empty struct fields like `visibility`, `author`, and `updateAuthor` are being included as empty objects (`{}`) even though they're marked with `omitempty`. This causes the Jira API to reject the request.

Here's the current struct definition:
```go
type Comment struct {
    // ... other fields ...
    Author       User              `json:"author,omitempty"`
    UpdateAuthor User              `json:"updateAuthor,omitempty"`
    Visibility   CommentVisibility `json:"visibility,omitempty"`
    // ... other fields ...
}
```

The problem shows up clearly in this Go playground example: https://go.dev/play/p/7DCOpLbUdq4

I've found that changing these fields to pointers (like `*User` and `*CommentVisibility`) fixes the issue because then `omitempty` properly omits the fields when they're nil. Can you confirm if this is the best approach or suggest any alternative solutions? I want to make sure we're not missing any edge cases with this pointer approach.

ds.zh_vibe_query:
我在通过我们的 Go client 向 Jira issue 添加评论时遇到了一个问题。将评论数据序列化为 JSON 时，像 `visibility`、`author` 和 `updateAuthor` 这样的空 struct 字段，尽管标记了 `omitempty`，仍然会被包含为空对象（`{}`）。这会导致 Jira API 拒绝该请求。

这是当前的 struct 定义：
```go
type Comment struct {
    // ... other fields ...
    Author       User              `json:"author,omitempty"`
    UpdateAuthor User              `json:"updateAuthor,omitempty"`
    Visibility   CommentVisibility `json:"visibility,omitempty"`
    // ... other fields ...
}
```

这个问题在这个 Go playground 示例中表现得很明显：https://go.dev/play/p/7DCOpLbUdq4

我发现把这些字段改为指针（例如 `*User` 和 `*CommentVisibility`）可以修复这个问题，因为这样 `omitempty` 就会在字段为 nil 时正确地省略这些字段。你能确认这是否是最佳做法，或者建议其他可选方案吗？我想确保这种指针方案没有遗漏任何边界情况。

